<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Areopagus of Eastern Continental Greece</h1><p class="st-meta">1821 CE – 1822 CE · capital Salona</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Regional revolutionary government of eastern mainland Greece in 1821-1822, set up at Salona under Theodoros Negris.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Eastern mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocis">Phocis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locris">Locris</a>, joined the revolution in 1821. In November 1821 an assembly of local representatives met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amfissa">Salona</a> (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-salona">Amfissa</a>) and, under the guidance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phanariotes">Phanariot</a> diplomat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoros-negris">Theodoros Negris</a>, adopted a legal charter and created a governing council named after the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/areopagus">Athenian Areopagus</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/areopagus">Areopagus</a> was made up of local notables and was meant to run the administration, justice and war effort in the region. It struggled to control powerful armed chieftains, above all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odysseas-androutsos">Odysseas Androutsos</a>, with whom it was in open conflict. Its authority over the scattered and contested territory was limited.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/epidaurus">Epidaurus</a> created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-hellenic-republic">First Hellenic Republic</a> in January 1822, the regional bodies were subordinated to central government. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/areopagus">Areopagus</a> continued for a time but lost its role during 1822 and 1823.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/areopagus-of-eastern-continental-greece.jpg" alt="Areopagus of Eastern Continental Greece" width="320" height="198"><figcaption>Image: vectorization by Anzee · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Areios_Pagos_Anatolikis_Ellados.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1821 CE – 1822 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Salona</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Theodoros Negris</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Areios Pagos of Eastern Greece</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1822&amp;focus=areopagus-of-eastern-continental-greece" aria-label="Areopagus of Eastern Continental Greece on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5236 795 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Areopagus of Eastern Continental Greece lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5556 1051L5709 970M5556 1051L5570 1082"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5570 1082h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5556 1051h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5556 1051h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Salona. <a href="/atlas?year=1822&amp;focus=areopagus-of-eastern-continental-greece">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
